<section class="principles section" aria-labelledby="principles-title">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">The direction</p><h2 id="principles-title">More control.<br>More room to choose.</h2><p>The aim is to keep your data and identity yours, make providers replaceable, and give you a way back when something fails.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="principle-list">
    <article>
      <span class="index">01</span>
      <div>
        <h3>Private</h3><p>You decide who can access your data and what they can do with it. Privacy begins with control and clear boundaries; it is never an absolute security guarantee.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article>
      <span class="index">02</span>
      <div>
        <h3>Decentralized</h3><p>Ownership belongs across individuals and businesses. Providers should be replaceable, so changing a service does not mean surrendering your identity or starting over.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article>
      <span class="index">03</span>
      <div>
        <h3>Open-source</h3><p>Software you can inspect and adapt offers a path to continuity beyond one vendor. The goal is to keep the tools useful—and maintainable—on your terms.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article>
      <span class="index">04</span>
      <div>
        <h3>Agent-first</h3><p>Design for useful agent assistance from the start: explicit permissions, understandable actions, and a person in control. Reliable assistance has to be demonstrated, not assumed.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="believe section" aria-labelledby="believe-title">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">What I believe</p><h2 id="believe-title">Own the machine.<br>Keep what the cloud got right.</h2><p>A restaurant should be able to run its own floor, and still reach it from anywhere.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="principle-list">
    <article>
      <span class="index">01</span>
      <div>
        <h3>Your data is yours.</h3><p>Records live on a machine you own, in one file you can copy and take with you.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article>
      <span class="index">02</span>
      <div>
        <h3>Nothing leaves unless you say so.</h3><p>Optional network features start switched off, and only the owner turns them on.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article>
      <span class="index">03</span>
      <div>
        <h3>Facts about people, never judgments.</h3><p>Every open check is visible to the whole team. Accountability comes from a record of who did what.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article>
      <span class="index">04</span>
      <div>
        <h3>The AI is optional. The math never is.</h3><p>Every number comes from code, so the same sales give the same answer.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="offline-passage section" aria-labelledby="offline-title">
  <p class="eyebrow">Reliability</p>
  <h2 id="offline-title">The internet goes down. Service doesn’t.</h2>
  <p>Built to keep the floor working when the internet doesn’t. Offline-first doesn’t need a native app. It needs the server to be yours.</p>
  <p class="status">In progress · <a class="text-link" href="/work/">What is and isn’t established yet <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>
</section>
